{"name":"Flapper Dance","hex":"#495762","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flapper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young girl usually between the ages of 15 and 18, especially one not \"out\" socially.","A young woman, especially when unconventional or without decorum or displaying daring freedom or boldness; now particularly associated with the Jazz Age of the 1920s. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who or that which flaps.","A young game bird just able to fly, particularly a wild duck."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flapper"},{"term":"dance","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sequence of rhythmic steps or movements usually performed to music, for pleasure or as a form of social interaction.","A social gathering where dancing is the main activity."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move with rhythmic steps or movements, especially in time to music.","To leap or move lightly and rapidly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Flapper","blocks":[{"text":"Flappers were a subculture of young Western women prominent after the First World War and through the 1920s who wore knee-length skirts, bobbed their hair, listened to jazz, and flaunted their disdain for prevailing codes of decent behavior. Flappers have been seen as brash for wearing excessive makeup, drinking alcohol, smoking cigarettes in public, driving automobiles, treating sex in a casual manner, and otherwise flouting social and sexual norms. As automobiles became more available, flappers gained freedom of movement and privacy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Louise_Brooks_ggbain_32453u_crop.jpg/330px-Louise_Brooks_ggbain_32453u_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flapper","wikidata":"Q1483126"},{"title":"Dance","blocks":[{"text":"Dance is an art form, consisting of sequences of body movements with aesthetic and often symbolic value, either improvised or purposefully selected. Dance can be categorized and described by its choreography, by its repertoire of movements or by its historical period or place of origin. Dance is typically performed with musical accompaniment, and sometimes with the dancer simultaneously using a musical instrument themselves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Two_dancers.jpg/330px-Two_dancers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance","wikidata":"Q11639"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/FlapperOnShip1929_crop.jpg/250px-FlapperOnShip1929_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2c/FlapperOnShip1929_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/FlapperOnShip1929_crop.jpg/250px-FlapperOnShip1929_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlapperOnShip1929_crop.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Violet_Romer_in_flapper_dress%2C_LC-DIG-ggbain-12393_crop.jpg/500px-Violet_Romer_in_flapper_dress%2C_LC-DIG-ggbain-12393_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Violet_Romer_in_flapper_dress%2C_LC-DIG-ggbain-12393_crop.jpg/1280px-Violet_Romer_in_flapper_dress%2C_LC-DIG-ggbain-12393_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Violet_Romer_in_flapper_dress%2C_LC-DIG-ggbain-12393_crop.jpg/500px-Violet_Rome